Spoilers...

Spell casting monsters of level 21 and above (including all
arch-liches, some other liches, Rodney, and several named demons but
not "clerical" spell casters like high priests) can cast "touch of
death".  If the spell succeeds, it will normally kill you instantly.
Fortunately, magic resistance provides total protection.

The details are as follows.  If you're polymorphed into a demon or
something nonliving (undead, golem, vortex, or manes), there's no
effect: "You seem no deader than before."  If you have magic
resistance, the spell always fails: "Lucky for you, it didn't work!"
Even without MR, there's a 12-in-monster's-level chance the spell will
fail, and you get the same message as with MR.  Otherwise, the spell
succeeds.  If you're hallucinating, then "You have an out of body
experience." and *survive*, oddly enough, and if you're not
hallucinating, you die.

